// Source for /img/display_autoruns.png, embedded by
// docs/developer_guides/data_fetching.md under "The fetch autoruns".
//
// THE TABLE ABOVE IT IS GENERATED AND THIS IS NOT THE SAME PICTURE. That table
// has one row per autorun -- name, trigger, action -- which is everything
// except the two facts a reader with an unexplained refetch needs: that three
// of the four converge, and that what they converge on re-enters the fourth. A
// row cannot say either, because both are about the relationship between rows.
// So this figure draws only trigger, autorun, action and that loop, and leaves
// the wording of each to the table beside it.
//
// THE CYCLE IS THE FIGURE, and `cancelFetch()` is where it closes. The three
// autoruns that end in a reset reach it through two of them rather than one:
// `clearAllRpcData()` drops `loadedRegions` and the canvas with it, while
// `invalidateSettings()` leaves both standing, so the held data draws under the
// `staleSettingsDrawn` scrim until the refetch lands. What they share is the
// cancel, and a cancel bumps `fetchGeneration`, which is a trigger of
// `FetchVisibleRegions` -- so every reset ends in a fetch, and "why did this
// refetch" is answered by naming which of the three ran. Drawn as the one
// dashed edge, the way dashed means "look again" in fetch_chain.dot.
//
// WHAT IT DELIBERATELY LEAVES OUT is `loadedRegions` and the display's own
// `rpcDataMap`, which look like the obvious middle of the picture. The fetch
// autorun reads both UNTRACKED (see the install site's comments: tracking
// loaded data would re-fire the autorun mid-fetch, and `fetchGeneration` at
// fetch end is the real re-trigger). A state node with a read edge into
// `FetchVisibleRegions` would draw a dependency MobX does not have, in the one
// figure whose whole subject is what depends on what.
//
// `clearByteEstimate()` is off it for a different reason: the byte estimate is
// dropped on this same `view.displayedRegions` trigger, but by
// `ClearByteEstimateOnNavOrTierSwap`, which `RegionTooLargeMixin` installs.
// Hanging it off `DisplayedRegionsChange` would name the wrong autorun, and
// this figure is scoped to the four `installPerRegionFetchAutoruns` installs.
//
// It also stops at `fetchNeeded(needed)`, which is where fetch_chain.dot
// starts. That figure's name is on the edge, in courier, the convention
// dataflow.dot uses for every crossing into a sibling figure.
//
// THE AUTORUN NODE IDS ARE THE AUTORUN NAMES, quoted -- and that is a contract,
// not a style. `generateFetchAutorunDocs.ts` reads the names structurally off
// the install calls to write the table above, and then checks this file for
// each one, so a fifth autorun cannot join the table while the figure keeps
// saying four. A quoted id here is an autorun name; everything else uses a bare
// id.
//
// LEFT TO RIGHT, which is the exception among the pipeline figures here (their
// header comments each record coming off a strip too wide to read). This one is
// four shallow columns rather than a chain, so the long axis is the SHORT one:
// stacked it is a narrow column four autoruns tall with the trigger names
// wrapped, and the funnel -- three autoruns, two resets, one cancel -- is what
// the figure is for.
digraph display_autoruns {
  rankdir=LR
  labelloc=t
  fontname="Helvetica"
  fontsize=18
  label="The fetch autoruns of a linear display: what wakes each one, and where it ends"
  nodesep=0.3
  ranksep=0.6

  node [shape=box style="filled,rounded" fillcolor="#ffffff" color="#9e9e9e"
        fontname="Helvetica" fontsize=12 margin="0.18,0.10"]
  edge [color="#555555" fontname="Helvetica" fontsize=10]

  // ── What changes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  node [fillcolor="#e1f5fe" color="#90caf9"]
  t_regions [label="view.displayedRegions"]
  t_settings [label="settingsFetchInputs"]
  t_view [label="view.visibleRegions"]
  t_gen [label="fetchGeneration\nreloadCounter"]

  // Pinned, because the row order decides where the dashed cycle edge below can
  // run: left to dot, `SettingsInvalidate` lands on the bottom row and the
  // return sweep crosses it under its own label.
  { rank=same; t_regions -> t_view -> t_settings -> t_gen [style=invis] }

  // ── The autoruns ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  node [shape=ellipse fillcolor="#f1f8e9" color="#aed581"]
  "DisplayedRegionsChange" [label="DisplayedRegionsChange"]
  "SettingsInvalidate" [label="SettingsInvalidate"]
  "ClearBlockingStateOnViewportChange" [label="ClearBlockingState\nOnViewportChange"]
  "FetchVisibleRegions" [label="FetchVisibleRegions\nimmediate, then 600 ms"]

  // ── What they do ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  clear [shape=box style="filled,rounded" fillcolor="#fff9c4" color="#ffe082"
         label="clearAllRpcData()"]
  invalidate [shape=box style="filled,rounded" fillcolor="#fff9c4" color="#ffe082"
              label="invalidateSettings()"]
  cancel [shape=box style="filled,rounded" fillcolor="#fff9c4" color="#ffe082"
          label="cancelFetch()"]
  fetch [shape=box style="filled,rounded" fillcolor="#dcedc8" color="#aed581"
         label="fetchNeeded(needed)"]

  t_regions -> "DisplayedRegionsChange"
  t_settings -> "SettingsInvalidate"
  t_view -> "ClearBlockingStateOnViewportChange"
  t_view -> "FetchVisibleRegions"
  t_gen -> "FetchVisibleRegions"

  "DisplayedRegionsChange" -> clear
  "SettingsInvalidate" -> invalidate
  // The one conditional trigger, and the condition is what the autorun is for:
  // a viewport move while a terminal flag is set is the only thing that lifts
  // it, since the too-large gate is derived and releases itself.
  "ClearBlockingStateOnViewportChange" -> clear [label="  error or fetchCanceled  "]
  "FetchVisibleRegions" -> fetch [label=<  uncovered blocks<br align="left"/>  <font face="Courier" color="#6b6b6b">fetch_chain</font><br align="left"/>>]

  clear -> cancel
  invalidate -> cancel

  // The cycle. constraint=false so closing it does not pull `t_gen` right and
  // fold the trigger column into the action column.
  cancel -> t_gen [style=dashed constraint=false label="  fetchGeneration++  "]
}
